# Print a few random numbers in [0, 1).
#
# `random` is a capability the host resolves — so the numbers differ each run. Pass `--seed N`
# to get the same sequence every time (the "same maze every time" flag):
#
#   doodle run examples/gallery/random.doodle
#   doodle run examples/gallery/random.doodle --seed 42

print("Three random numbers in [0, 1):")
print(random())
print(random())
print(random())
